course: dictionary
lesson: 5014
title: Inflammation: the body's alarm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inflammation is what happens when part of your body is hurt or fighting germs. The area goes red, swollen, hot and sore. «Inflammation, redness, warmth and swelling, is the body sending blood and white cells to fight germs.» The clue words redness, warmth and swelling all describe a body part that is working hard.
explain: Inflammation is not the germs themselves. It is the body's own defence reaction, the way it sends extra blood and helper cells to a damaged place. Think of it like sending extra helpers to mend a broken fence.
explain: Doctors use the word in illness names too. Many names ending in «-itis» mean inflammation of a body part, such as tonsillitis, appendicitis and conjunctivitis. Phrases like «reduce inflammation» tell you the body is calming down, and «signs of inflammation» tell you what to look for.
fact: Inflammation means part of the body becomes red, swollen, hot and painful.
fact: It usually happens because the body is hurt or is fighting an infection.
fact: Inflammation is the body's defence reaction that brings extra blood and helper cells to a damaged place.
fact: Many illness names ending in «-itis» mean inflammation: tonsillitis, appendicitis, conjunctivitis.
fact: If redness spreads or a fever comes with it, a doctor should check it.
exercise: A sprained ankle swells, feels hot and is sore. What is this an example of? | A cold draught | Dehydration | *Inflammation | A broken bone that has healed
exercise: Which ending in an illness name means inflammation? | *-itis | -ful | -ology | -ness
exercise: «Inflammation, redness, warmth and swelling, is the body sending blood and white cells to fight germs.» What does the body send to fight germs? | *Blood and white cells | Sweets and water | Rain and wind | Air and dust
test: Which word means the red, hot, swollen and painful reaction of the body to injury or infection? | Respiration | Digestion | *Inflammation | Hibernation
test: What should you do if redness spreads and you also have a fever? | *Tell a grown-up and see a doctor | Rub the area hard | Ignore it and go to sleep | Wait for it to get dark
exam: Which of these is an illness name that means inflammation? | Fever | *Appendicitis | Sprain | Bruise
